codex
The bare harness exhausted the OpenRouter key after proving both `easy` and `medium` too easy, but before it could score `hard`. Independently, the placebo diagnostic solved the current hard rung once, so I’m strengthening the named ladder to the most obscured fixed-answer-length setting already supported by the construction, then re-running every local gate.
exec
/bin/bash -lc "python3 - <<'PY'
import gen_2005_13608 as g, time
p={'n':72,'guide_gap':11,'mix_rounds':128}
t=time.perf_counter(); bad=[]
for seed in range(100):
 try:
  i=g.make_instance(seed=seed,**p)
  ok,why=g.verify(i,i['answer'])
  if not ok: bad.append((seed,why))
 except Exception as e: bad.append((seed,str(e)))
print('tested=100 bad=',len(bad),'elapsed=',round(time.perf_counter()-t,3),bad[:5])
PY" in /home/gson/gvrepo/results/2005.13608
