Built and locally verified a Track B generator based on Section 3, Theorem 10 of the [paper](https://arxiv.org/abs/2005.13608).

- Module: [gen_2005_13608.py](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/2005.13608/gen_2005_13608.py:37)
- Gate evidence: [selftest_report.json](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/2005.13608/selftest_report.json)
- Documentation: [README.md](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/2005.13608/README.md:1)
- Partial bare oracle transcript: [llm_loop_transcript.jsonl](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/2005.13608/llm_loop_transcript.jsonl)
- G9 transcripts: [hinted](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/2005.13608/g9_hinted_transcript.jsonl), [placebo](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/2005.13608/g9_placebo_transcript.jsonl)

Local results:

- All G1–G9 local gates pass.
- Random guessing: 0/200,000.
- Exact valid fraction: approximately `1.1856e-7`.
- Five adversarial attacks: each 0/8.
- Reference algorithm: up to 1,273,144 word operations.
- Compact route: 284 operations.
- Answer: 25 characters and 6 atoms.
- Deterministic across Python hash seeds.

The only blocker is external: OpenRouter exhausted its key limit after proving `easy` solved 3/3 and `medium` solved 2/3, before scoring `hard`. Therefore `.meta.json` has no hardened verdict and the result is not submission-ready. G9 recorded hinted 1/3 and placebo 1/3, giving a diagnostic difference of `0.0`.

After restoring OpenRouter capacity, rerun:

```bash
cd /home/gson/gvrepo/results/2005.13608
python3 ../../scripts/harden.py gen_2005_13608.py
```

No `REJECTED.md` was created because this is an infrastructure block, not a failure of G, H, or V.
